    "chunk_size_bytes": 2002,
    "chunk_text": "Access Real Estate partners with Chaminda Vaas to drive nationwide expansion\n\nAccess Real Estate, a prominent subsidiary of the Access group, yesterday officially appointed legendary Sri Lankan cricketer Chaminda Vaas as its Brand Ambassador, aligning with the company\u2019s landmark 15th anniversary celebrations.\n\nThe strategic partnership anchors a new era of growth for the property developer, which aims to aggressively expand its footprint into new geographical districts across Sri Lanka.\n\nSince its inception in 2011, the company has grown into a major industry player, successfully delivering more than 155 developments spanning over 350 acres of land and securing a loyal customer base of over 4,500 landowners.\n\nThe collaboration is designed to spearhead the company\u2019s next phase of business expansion, moving beyond its traditional strongholds into new regional markets.\n\nAccess Real Estate specialises in developing fully-serviced, ready-to-build residential and commercial plots, equipped with modern infrastructure, including three-phase electricity, pipe-borne water and wide internal roads situated near major economic hubs.\n\nBy aligning with Vaas, the company plans to scale its operations manifold, leveraging his massive public appeal and trusted reputation to reach the hearts of consumers in untapped markets across the island.\n\nReflecting on the milestone and the company\u2019s forward-looking expansion strategy, Access Real Estate Managing Director and CEO Theo Fernando noted that the partnership reflects the core values of the institution.\n\n\u201cReaching our 15-year milestone is a testament to the trust our clients place in us. Welcoming Chaminda Vaas to the Access Real Estate family is the perfect way to celebrate. Chaminda represents the pinnacle of Sri Lankan dedication, consistency and excellence, the exact pillars upon which we develop our projects,\u201d Fernando stated, highlighting the company\u2019s commitment to venturing into new pathways and achieving new heights."
